 "result": "I wrote `ANSWER.txt` in the repository root. The function is `parse_basic_str_escape` in `src/tomli/_parser.py`.\n\n- **Callers:** `parse_basic_str` calls it for both string kinds. Multi-line strings go through the thin wrapper `parse_basic_str_escape_multiline`, which passes `multiline=True`. That flag enables the line-ending backslash that skips whitespace.\n- **`\\uXXXX` handling:** On `\\u`, it calls `parse_hex_char` to read exactly 4 hex digits. It raises `TOMLDecodeError` for invalid hex or for values that aren't Unicode scalar values, such as surrogates. Otherwise it returns `chr()` of the code point.\n\nI didn't open `parse_one_line_basic_str` (line 516). I'm assuming it hands off to `parse_basic_str`, so I haven't confirmed that single-line strings reach the escape function that way.",
